WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.550
Our first guest wrote in with a special request.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:07.120
Ruby Ortiz is an 11th-grade Spanish teacher in Brooklyn,

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.330
but today, she's putting down the textbooks and picking up

4
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:14.840
the microphone to be our co-host for the day.

5
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.117
Ruby, welcome.

6
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:16.950
(audience applauds)

7
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.918
Thank you.

8
00:00:17.918 --> 00:00:19.168
Thanks so much.

9
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.910
Well, Drew, I am really excited to be here.

10
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.940
I love watching your show after a long day of work.

11
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.580
I mean, I love your Stan for Stains segment.

12
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.960
You've helped me remove so many stains.

13
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.793
I love it.

14
00:00:33.793 --> 00:00:36.570
You host so many fabulous celebrities.

15
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.390
I love to be here.

16
00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.730
I hope that by being here,

17
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.950
I can show my students that you can do anything

18
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.320
you put your mind to,

19
00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.218
and I'm excited to get started and ready to be here.

20
00:00:46.218 --> 00:00:49.858
(audience applauds)

21
00:00:49.858 --> 00:00:53.250
Well, we sent you home last night

22
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.420
with a whole bunch of what we call dossiers,

23
00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:00.559
which just sounds like Oprah Winfrey meets the FBI.

24
00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:01.490
(audience laughs)

25
00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.110
It's like on our show,

26
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.450
we have a lot of information on everyone who comes.

27
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.210
Everything goes into these dossiers.

28
00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.030
So we gave you our homework packet last night.

29
00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:11.863
You did.

30
00:01:11.863 --> 00:01:12.696
I'm ready.

31
00:01:12.696 --> 00:01:15.080
I've studied my notes, and I'm ready for today.

32
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.520
All right, then you and me both.

33
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:17.480
All right, well let's head over

34
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:19.828
to the news desk to hit the headlines.

35
00:01:19.828 --> 00:01:23.810
(upbeat music)
(audience applauds)

36
00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.490
Okay, it's time for Drew's News,

37
00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:28.050
your daily tip of the good news cap.

38
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.550
And with me at the desk is one of the finest fellows

39
00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.219
in news, Ross Mathews.

40
00:01:32.219 --> 00:01:33.052
Hi.

41
00:01:33.052 --> 00:01:33.885
Hi, everybody.

42
00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:34.766
(audience applauds)

43
00:01:34.766 --> 00:01:35.599
Hi, Drew.

44
00:01:36.488 --> 00:01:37.770
(Ross laughs)

45
00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.220
Oh, this is so fun.

46
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.490
I love kicking off the show with the news.

47
00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.970
I know, and we got a lot to talk about today.

48
00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.280
So here we go.

49
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:48.280
First up, fans of the classic horror movie franchise

50
00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.980
Halloween are freaking out,

51
00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:53.330
because the new movie comes out Friday.

52
00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.163
Ooh.

53
00:01:54.163 --> 00:01:56.680
I know. Halloween Kills stars the legendary

54
00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.450
scream queen, Jamie Lee Curtis,

55
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:02.090
and of course the always creepy Michael Myers.

56
00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:04.030
(audience laughs)

57
00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:06.000
No one's more excited than a little

58
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.730
four-year-old girl named Aria.

59
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.310
She recently went viral,

60
00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.860
because she was simply over the moon

61
00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.950
when Michael Myers crashed her birthday.

62
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:14.887
What?

63
00:02:14.887 --> 00:02:15.720
(audience laughs)

64
00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.553
Look at this.

65
00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:19.483
Yeah. She loves him, apparently-

66
00:02:19.483 --> 00:02:20.316
(Ross groans)

67
00:02:20.316 --> 00:02:22.333
and he's her favorite character.

68
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:24.970
I don't know how in the hell she

69
00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:29.290 line:15%
found out about him in the first place, but yeah.

70
00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:31.572 line:15%
(Ross groans)

71
00:02:31.572 --> 00:02:33.070 line:15%
Rossy, what would you do if Michael Myers

72
00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.240 line:15%
showed up to your birthday?

73
00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.550 line:15%
I'd be chucking cupcakes,

74
00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.383 line:15%
is what I be doing.

75
00:02:36.383 --> 00:02:37.216 line:15%
Get out of here.
(audience laughs)

76
00:02:37.216 --> 00:02:39.720 line:15%
You know I don't like scary movies, okay.

77
00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.410
The scariest movie I ever watched was Mrs. Doubtfire.

78
00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.501
I don't like anything worse than that.

79
00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:45.334
(Drew laughs)
(audience laughs)

80
00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.440
This little girl, can we get her a Barney?

81
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.340
Something.

82
00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.340
This is freaky.

83
00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:50.173
No, ma'am.

84
00:02:50.173 --> 00:02:51.185
No, no.

85
00:02:51.185 --> 00:02:52.018
(audience laughs)

86
00:02:52.018 --> 00:02:53.170
Well, do you know what's really funny-

87
00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:54.003
What?

88
00:02:54.003 --> 00:02:56.630
is my daughter Frankie loves "It".

89
00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.310
That movie, "It"?

90
00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.270
Well, not the movie, because

91
00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:00.850
I don't want her to watch the movie.

92
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:01.683
What is "It"?

93
00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:04.666
It's that clown who is a killer.

94
00:03:04.666 --> 00:03:05.499
(blows raspberries)

95
00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:06.870
Out, timeout, got to go.

96
00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.215
Nope, nope!

97
00:03:08.215 --> 00:03:09.048
(audience laughs)

98
00:03:09.048 --> 00:03:11.770
And she knows he's dark, but she also loves cemeteries.

99
00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.260
She's a little macabre.

100
00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.291
You know what I mean?

101
00:03:14.291 --> 00:03:15.124
Oh, God.

102
00:03:15.124 --> 00:03:17.000
Ruby, are you a horror movie fan?

103
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:17.833
I'm not.

104
00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:18.666
I'm with Ross.

105
00:03:18.666 --> 00:03:19.803
I am not a fan.

106
00:03:19.803 --> 00:03:20.670
Yeah.

107
00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:22.640
I can't sit through a scary movie.

108
00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.460
I'm jumping every five seconds.

109
00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.293
I can't.

110
00:03:25.293 --> 00:03:26.126
My heart's racing.

111
00:03:26.126 --> 00:03:27.280
Ruby and I'll be in the corner watching

112
00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:28.541
Pretty Woman on a loop.

113
00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.540
Yes we will.
Thank you.

114
00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:30.448
(Ruby laughs)
(audience laughs)

115
00:03:30.448 --> 00:03:31.281
Thank you.

116
00:03:31.281 --> 00:03:32.114
Yes we will.

117
00:03:32.114 --> 00:03:33.000
Well, speaking of Halloween classics,

118
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.060
Tim Burton's "The Nightmare Before Christmas",

119
00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.273
have you seen it?

120
00:03:36.273 --> 00:03:38.714
(audience cheers)

121
00:03:38.714 --> 00:03:40.478
Well, then you're in luck.

122
00:03:40.478 --> 00:03:41.311
It's going to be turned into a

123
00:03:41.311 --> 00:03:43.480
live concert film event this month.

124
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.860
And People reports that the

125
00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:47.270
beloved character of Sally will be performed

126
00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:50.366
by none other than Billie Eilish.

127
00:03:50.366 --> 00:03:51.835
My favorite!
(audience cheers)

128
00:03:51.835 --> 00:03:52.816
Right?

129
00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:53.900 line:15%
My favorite.

130
00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.220 line:15%
Great casting.

131
00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.240 line:15%
My hero.

132
00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:57.210 line:15%
My favorite.

133
00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.700 line:15%
Yeah, she's going to be phenomenal in this,

134
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.110 line:15%
and she'll perform with the incredible Danny Elfman,

135
00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.090 line:15%
reprising Jack Skellington.

136
00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.870 line:15%
And you've seen this, right?

137
00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:06.800 line:15%
You like "Nightmare Before Christmas"?

138
00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.090 line:15%
I do love this movie.

139
00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.610
Big Tim Burton fan.

140
00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.450
I would say my favorite Tim Burton movie

141
00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.000
probably still to this day is "Edward Scissorhands".

142
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.590
Oh, yes.

143
00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.640
And "Beetlejuice".

144
00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:18.920
I love "Beetlejuice".

145
00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.490
I auditioned for Beetlejuice.

146
00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:21.323
Wait, time out.

147
00:04:21.323 --> 00:04:22.700
You auditioned for "Beetlejuice"?

148
00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.830
Oh, I audition for everything.

149
00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.560
The main character, Winona?

150
00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.393
Yes.

151
00:04:28.393 --> 00:04:29.226
Wow.

152
00:04:29.226 --> 00:04:30.074
Yes.

153
00:04:30.074 --> 00:04:32.010
I have auditioned for every movie out there.

154
00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:32.843
Really?
(audience laughs)

155
00:04:32.843 --> 00:04:34.060
Absolutely.

156
00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.387
Oh, I have so many more questions.

157
00:04:35.387 --> 00:04:36.550
When I was a kid, yeah.

158
00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:39.100
What one killed you the most that you didn't get?

159
00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.160
Gosh, that's a good question.

160
00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.798
I don't know.

161
00:04:44.798 --> 00:04:46.790
(stammers)

162
00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:48.706
I mean, I auditioned for "Cape Fear".

163
00:04:48.706 --> 00:04:49.577
Oh.

164
00:04:49.577 --> 00:04:50.410
I told that story.

165
00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.868
Yeah.

166
00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:52.701
That's what happens.

167
00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:54.640
You know, you just try out for everything.

168
00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:55.490
Well, I'm still upset

169
00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.230
they didn't cast me as James Bond, but you know what?

170
00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.307
I move on.

171
00:04:58.307 --> 00:04:59.230
(Drew laughs)
(audience laughs)

172
00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:00.356
Got over it.

173
00:05:00.356 --> 00:05:02.110
(Drew laughs)

174
00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:03.570
I should say yet.

175
00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.830
They haven't cast me yet as James Bond.

176
00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:08.540
They're looking for a new one, Rossy.

177
00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.083
That's a double "Oh no."

178
00:05:10.083 --> 00:05:12.740
(Drew laughs)
(audience laughs)

179
00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.100
Well, we've got some good news

180
00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:18.914
from the golden arches in today's Green News.

181
00:05:18.914 --> 00:05:21.250
(audience applauds)

182
00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:24.510
I'm very excited about this.

183
00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:27.040
PBS reports that McDonald's has made a pledge

184
00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:30.270
to drastically cut the use of plastics in

185
00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.540
Happy Meal toys.

186
00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.670
Yes!

187
00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:34.115
I love this!

188
00:05:34.115 --> 00:05:35.384
(audience applauds)

189
00:05:35.384 --> 00:05:39.850
By 2025, they will use 90% less plastic,

190
00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.720
and they're already phasing in toys

191
00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:44.440 line:15%
made of cardboard and plant-based plastics.

192
00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:48.080 line:15%
And also by 2025, all of their food packaging

193
00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.489 line:15%
will be in sustainable and fully-recyclable boxes.

194
00:05:51.489 --> 00:05:52.322 line:15%
(audience applauds)

195
00:05:52.322 --> 00:05:53.155 line:15%
Oh, this is great.

196
00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:59.060
I say this a lot, but I'm going to keep saying it.

197
00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:02.330
I am scared that we will not make this deadline

198
00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:03.470
to save our planet.

199
00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.560
And when the big companies step in and say

200
00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.920
they're going to make the changes, I get hopeful.

201
00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:09.031
Yeah.

202
00:06:09.031 --> 00:06:11.660 line:15%
Because we have to make our individual efforts,

203
00:06:13.895 --> 00:06:16.700 line:15%
but it feels futile when the big companies

204
00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:17.950
are doing it a different way.

205
00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.760
So thank you, McDonald's.

206
00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.430
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

207
00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:24.290
I very much, as one citizen, really appreciate it.

208
00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:25.320
Yeah, I do too.

209
00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.153
And I have to say,

210
00:06:26.153 --> 00:06:27.420
I was a little hesitant though,

211
00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.410
because this is great that they're doing this,

212
00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.810
but here's a nugget of advice, McDonald's.

213
00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.900
You got to keep them cool.

214
00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:34.733
Right?

215
00:06:34.733 --> 00:06:35.566
Because when I was a little kid,

216
00:06:35.566 --> 00:06:38.300
I would go to town on a Happy Meal for that toy.

217
00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.270
And I have to say, we have some of them right here.

218
00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:42.270
Well done, McDonald's.

219
00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.980
They're cool, all right?

220
00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:44.813
Look at this.

221
00:06:44.813 --> 00:06:46.001
It's cute.

222
00:06:46.001 --> 00:06:46.834
It's all paper.

223
00:06:46.834 --> 00:06:47.667
I'd be excited about this.

224
00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:49.040
Listen, this is just good news.

225
00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:49.873
I'm into it.

226
00:06:49.873 --> 00:06:51.430
Me too, yeah.

227
00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.856
But just keep them cool like this, okay?

228
00:06:53.856 --> 00:06:54.718
This is cool.

229
00:06:54.718 --> 00:06:55.551
Or I'm hitting Burger King on the way home.

230
00:06:55.551 --> 00:06:56.384
Got it?

231
00:06:56.384 --> 00:06:57.217
(audience laughs)

232
00:06:57.217 --> 00:06:58.370
Well, we have a new segment alert.

233
00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.550
We're trying something brand new today.

234
00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.200
We asked you what we should review,

235
00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.940
and we got so many good responses.

236
00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:08.490
So now it's time for the first-ever installment

237
00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:10.806
of Drew's Reviews.

238
00:07:10.806 --> 00:07:15.686
(synth sounds)
(audience cheers)

239
00:07:15.686 --> 00:07:17.246
Oh, it's warm.

240
00:07:17.246 --> 00:07:19.270
I swear, Ross is going to kill me.

241
00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:20.480
Every-
Every day I show up,

242
00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.080
there's a different carbohydrate here

243
00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.140
waiting for us to eat.

244
00:07:23.140 --> 00:07:24.970
I am trying to keep it together, Drew.

245
00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:26.136
I know.

246
00:07:26.136 --> 00:07:26.969
I'm sorry.

247
00:07:26.969 --> 00:07:27.802
And I was on a diet too,

248
00:07:27.802 --> 00:07:28.849
and now, oh gosh.

249
00:07:28.849 --> 00:07:29.682
Well, what are you going to do?

250
00:07:29.682 --> 00:07:30.515
Come on.

251
00:07:30.515 --> 00:07:31.348
Well, today, our pick comes from

252
00:07:31.348 --> 00:07:34.050
Rachael Oseland on Instagram.

253
00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:37.420 line:15%
It's Trader Joe's Pumpkin Caramel Kringle.

254
00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:40.770 line:15%
Now, apparently, the kringle is a Trader Joe's specialty,

255
00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:44.070 line:15%
but only during this special time of year

256
00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.530 line:15%
can you get it in the pumpkin flavor.

257
00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:47.840
By the way, I'm salivating.

258
00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.523
Okay, okay.

259
00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:51.373
How much did you eat?

260
00:07:51.373 --> 00:07:52.206
Did you lick it, Rossy?

261
00:07:52.206 --> 00:07:53.733
Did you take a lady bite?

262
00:07:53.733 --> 00:07:54.760
(audience laughs)

263
00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.770
I took a petite nibble, thank you very much.

264
00:07:57.770 --> 00:07:59.843
I took a giant mouthful of it.

265
00:08:02.045 --> 00:08:03.270
You know what it's giving me in a great way?

266
00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:04.333
Like maple bar.

267
00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:08.430
It's giving me cinnamon roll.

268
00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.690
Yeah, it's like the two of those mated.

269
00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:10.740
I'm not mad about it.

270
00:08:11.939 --> 00:08:12.780
Yeah, this is really good.

271
00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:15.130
